    "narrative": "**Lawrence Butler** stands out as the premier play for LawDog today, boasting an elite score of 73.47 against Littell. His projection is bolstered by a massive +13% platoon edge and a +10% park factor, making him a high-upside asset despite hitting in the bottom third of the order. Following closely is **Dylan Beavers** (64.32), whose value is inflated by the matchup against Arrighetti and a +4% efficiency boost derived from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a significant window for stolen base production\u2014a priority category for us. **Gavin Sheets** (62.32) and **JJ Bleday** (61.32) also land in the strong category, with the latter benefiting from a +14% park factor that compensates for his platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.06), who hovered just outside the starting rotation. While he offers a positive platoon split against Woo, he ultimately lost out to the higher raw efficiency of **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Luis Arraez**, whose presence atop the order provides more stability for run production. Meanwhile, **Bryce Harper** (59.48) remains a must-start despite a tougher matchup against Manaea; his elite xwOBA of 0.391 keeps his floor high enough to warrant a spot in the utility slot. We remain cautious with **Cal Raleigh** (52.21) today, as the matchup against Webb provides a negative platoon and park adjustment that pulls his score toward our marginal threshold. Owners should monitor all lineups closely, especially with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on our current depth to navigate today\u2019s 5x5 slate.",
